      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(3,5)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which point must lie on $y=-f(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=-f(x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(3,5)$ lies $5$ units *above* the $x$-axis. So, under the action of the transformation, this point will be reflected $5$ units *below* the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217907/assets/15c5cadbce652b40c2507fe9457ba9d836239c63e232e4924fe03a1615e76817.png)\n\nWe conclude that the point $(3,-5)$ must lie on the graph of $y=-f(x).$",
